  "details": "Hello, I run VRChat on PC since I am waiting to get a headset, but since the new update it has been crashing randomly. \nI can easily launch VRChat with no issues, be in my home world for a while and it'll be fine. Although, if I change my avatar, go to a new world, invite someone and they show up, or just wait for a while I will crash after a certain amount of time. It does the normal white fade and the, \"VRChat is not responding,\" and if I try to wait for it to respond it won't so I am forced to quit the program and relaunch.\nAt first I thought maybe it was Melonloader/EMMVRC so I removed them, but it still continues to crash. I uninsitalled VRChat from steam and reinstalled it, but nothing has seemed to work so far. So, because of this I'm not sure if it's the new update or if it's something to do with my files/ect.",
